      "content": "I'm sorry to hear that your pain is still unrelieved, but I must stress that taking 3000mg of Tylenol in one go could lead to serious side effects and potentially dangerous conditions such as liver damage, especially if you haven't taken anything in the past 24 hours. The maximum recommended daily dosage is 4000mg, but it should not be exceeded in a single dose and you should aim to maintain daily amounts not exceeding 3000mg for adults, divided throughout the day.\n\nGiven the intensity of your pain, it is crucial that you see a healthcare professional promptly for appropriate pain relief and treatment. In the meantime, you may consider using pain relief gels, rinse your mouth if you have an oral infection, or try applying pressure around the impacted tooth with spongy charcoal to alleviate pain. Remember, it's better to be safe and seek professional advice rather than risking your health.",
